 "note": "PASS at the standard gate (73/73 at dE 16; IoU min .863 mean .893, dE mean 13.02 max 15.6). REBUILT (rounds 18-19, 2026-09-29) as a muscular humanoid instead of the old egg body (61/73 but no arms, face or torso): gargoyle.py torso3 (one lathed V torso from torso_rings + flat pecs + the diagonal strap), face (brow, glints, snout, mouth + teeth), legs2 (thigh/knee/shin/clawed foot), the horns as elongated loops (horn_sx/sy), the arms RAISED to the horn loops (prior arm 130 for f12-f74), wings pleated as geometry (wing_pleats 5), a box-like cloak for the emergence. The source is TWO differently lit renders: f02-f41 (unfold + flap) and f42-f74 (the red-ball wind-up), so frame_opts gives f42-f74 kind g2 (its own body_gain/foot/pleat opts) and look per_kind fits each group's light. The open-wing frames f12-f38 take a harder light (look frame_opts gamma 0.8, key 3.6: dE -1 to -2 there, worse on the cloak frames and f39-f74). optim fix pins egg 0 for f02-f41 (else the optimiser hides a red ball in the cloak), cloak 0 for f18-f74, arm 25 / elbow 0 for f02-f10 (arm 0 dropped f03-f05 IoU to .83); f14 wrap 35 by hand (at 26 it matched source f23 better than f14 -> rank fail). Asm frames 1-0x49 = f02-f74: unfold f02-f18 (a frame per 6), flap CYCLE f18-f33, wind-up f33-f74 (a frame per 4). Round 25: a per-row silhouette bias (tmp/row_bias.py) showed the 3D 5 px narrower at SD rows 40-46 on the wind-up frames = the wings' lower membrane -> gargoyle.py opt wing_lo (px outward below y -10) = 2.5 on the g2 frames f42-f74 only (it costs IoU on the flap frames): IoU mean .882 -> .889, all 73 tween pairs kept. Round 26: the unfold frames f07-f11 showed the same narrow wing bottom (the source's wings hang as a box, 37 px wide down to row 58; ours tapered to 29), so wing_lo is now set per frame on f06-f41 as well -- a ramp 2, 5, 8 x4 (f08-f11), 4 x3, 3 x3, 2 x3 on f06-f20, 0 on the flap frames f21-f31 (where it costs IoU), 1, 2, 2 on f32-f34 and 4 on f35-f41: f09/f10 16.6/16.7 -> 15.6/15.3, every touched frame better, IoU mean .889 -> .893, all 73 tween pairs kept. The ball BURSTS (f67-f74, round 24): gargoyle.py burst_n 4 red chunks (frag_f / frag_long) spread on a horizontal ring and shrink as pose 'burst' goes 0 -> 1 (optim fix burst 0 on f02-f66; f74 egg_y held at -3 so the chunks stay above the head). Known differences: the chunks are smooth, the source's are ragged; the source's specular highlights (177-208) render at ~85-110; the wing's lower edge is a straight pleated trapezoid, not scalloped. Backups: tmp/fb_backup/Gargoyle_sprites/ (*_r18_pre = the old egg model).",
